[27.518862, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠦\u001b[0m Gathering context and asking the model...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[27.520468, "o", "\u001b[3m                                        1 failing test(s)                                         \u001b[0m\r\n┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━┳━━━━━━━━━━━━┓\r\n┃\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mTest                                         \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m┃\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mGuards                 \u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m┃\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1m   Rows\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m┃\u001b[1m \u001b[0m\u001b[1mConfidence\u001b[0m\u001b[1m \u001b[0m┃\r\n┡━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━╇━━━━━━━━━━━━┩\r\n│ assert_int_trips_enriched_speed_within_bounds │ main.int_trips_enriched │ 1826500 │ \u001b[32mhigh\u001b[0m       │\r"]
[27.520638, "o", "\n└───────────────────────────────────────────────┴─────────────────────────┴─────────┴────────────┘\r\n"]
[27.522264, "o", "\u001b[32m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[32m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[32m assert_int_trips_enriched_speed_within_bounds \u001b[0m\u001b[32m─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[32m─╮\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRoot cause\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m The avg_speed_mph formula uses a multiplier of 600 instead of 60. The formula is: round(600 * trip_distance / nullif(trip_duration_minutes, 0), 2). Since        \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m trip_duration_minutes is in minutes, the correct conversion to miles per hour requires multiplying by 60 (i.e., distance_miles / (duration_minutes / 60) =       \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m"]
[27.522317, "o", "│\u001b[0m distance_miles * 60 / duration_minutes). Using 600 instead of 60 inflates every computed speed by exactly 10x, which is confirmed by the sample data: e.g., a    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m trip of 1.91 miles in 10 minutes yields 600*1.91/10 = 114.6 mph shown in the data, whereas the correct calculation would be 60*1.91/10 = 11.46 mph — a plausible \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m city taxi speed. Similarly, 0.35 miles in 2 minutes gives 600*0.35/2 = 105.0 mph (shown), vs. the correct 60*0.35/2 = 10.5 mph. Every single failing row is      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m explained by this 10x inflation, and the test threshold of 80 mph is being exceeded solely because of the wrong multiplier.                                      \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1mSuggested fix\u001b[0m                                                       "]
[27.522325, "o", "                                                                                             \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m Change the multiplier in the avg_speed_mph calculation from 600 to 60 in the int_trips_enriched model:                                                           \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m   -- Before (incorrect):                                                                                                                                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m   round(600 * t.trip_distance / nullif(t.trip_duration_minutes, 0), 2) as avg_speed_mph                                                                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                         "]
[27.522336, "o", "         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m   -- After (correct):                                                                                                                                            \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m   round(60 * t.trip_distance / nullif(t.trip_duration_minutes, 0), 2) as avg_speed_mph                                                                           \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m This correctly converts (miles / minutes) to miles per hour by multiplying by 60 min/hr instead of 600.                                                          \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                                                                                  \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m \u001b[1mEvidence\u001b[0m                                "]
[27.522341, "o", "                                                                                                                         \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m Row 1: trip_distance=1.91, trip_duration_minutes=10, avg_speed_mph=114.6. Verification: 600*1.91/10=114.6 (matches exactly); 60*1.91/10=11.46 (plausible). Row   \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m 2: 0.35 miles / 2 min → 600*0.35/2=105.0 (matches exactly); correct=10.5 mph. Row 5 (LaGuardia): 10.1 miles / 31 min → 600*10.1/31=195.48 (matches exactly);     \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m correct=19.55 mph. All 20 sampled rows confirm the consistent 10x inflation caused by the 600 multiplier instead of 60. The failing row count of 1,826,500 is    \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m│\u001b[0m consistent with the entire dataset being affected by this systematic formula error.                                                                              \u001b[32m│\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[27.522514, "o", "\u001b[32m╰─\u001b[0m\u001b[32m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[32m confidence: high \u001b[0m\u001b[32m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[32m─╯\u001b[0m\r\n"]
